1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,180
Sooner or later, someone will
say: I never got your text.

2
00:00:04,180 --> 00:00:09,473
In this lesson, you'll learn a simple
four-step check that finds the reason almost

3
00:00:09,473 --> 00:00:13,088
every time, using Enrollment
History and Execution Logs.

4
00:00:13,949 --> 00:00:15,042
Here's the order.

5
00:00:15,042 --> 00:00:17,035
One, is the workflow published?

6
00:00:17,035 --> 00:00:19,349
Two, did the contact actually enrol?

7
00:00:19,349 --> 00:00:24,235
Three, if they didn't, does the trigger
and its filters match what happened?

8
00:00:24,235 --> 00:00:27,900
And four, what do the execution
logs say about each step?

9
00:00:28,791 --> 00:00:30,110
Start with the list.

10
00:00:30,110 --> 00:00:32,616
Open the folder, and check the status.

11
00:00:32,616 --> 00:00:35,452
Drafts never run, not
even for one contact.

12
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:40,728
It sounds obvious, but a workflow left
in draft after testing is the most common

13
00:00:40,728 --> 00:00:41,585
cause of all.

14
00:00:42,437 --> 00:00:46,207
Our first case: Grace Wright
filled in a form on the website,

15
00:00:46,207 --> 00:00:48,309
but never got the Invisalign text.

16
00:00:48,309 --> 00:00:51,152
Open Enrollment History,
and search for Grace.

17
00:00:51,152 --> 00:00:51,646
Nothing.

18
00:00:51,646 --> 00:00:56,158
She never entered the workflow at all,
so no step could ever run for her.

19
00:00:57,009 --> 00:01:00,237
When someone never enrolled,
look at the trigger.

20
00:01:00,237 --> 00:01:03,135
The filter says, form
is Invisalign Enquiry.

21
00:01:03,135 --> 00:01:06,231
Grace used the general
Contact Us form instead.

22
00:01:06,231 --> 00:01:09,195
So the workflow did
exactly what it was told.

23
00:01:09,195 --> 00:01:13,938
The fix is to add that form, or point
her to a workflow that handles it.

24
00:01:14,788 --> 00:01:19,468
Our second case: Mason Evans did
enrol, but says he never got a text.

25
00:01:19,468 --> 00:01:20,825
Open Execution Logs.

26
00:01:20,825 --> 00:01:25,030
Every step, for every contact,
is listed here with its status.

27
00:01:25,030 --> 00:01:28,286
Search for Mason, and
look at the status column.

28
00:01:29,137 --> 00:01:30,712
Most steps say Executed.

29
00:01:30,712 --> 00:01:33,009
But both text messages say Skipped.

30
00:01:33,009 --> 00:01:36,880
Skipped means Kyntlo chose not
to run that step on purpose.

31
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:40,030
Failed means it tried,
and something went wrong.

32
00:01:40,030 --> 00:01:41,736
They need different fixes.

33
00:01:42,586 --> 00:01:43,822
Click View details.

34
00:01:43,822 --> 00:01:48,246
Here's the reason: the contact has
Do Not Disturb turned on for SMS.

35
00:01:48,246 --> 00:01:51,304
Kyntlo respects that
setting in every workflow,

36
00:01:51,304 --> 00:01:54,947
which protects you from texting
people who've opted out.

37
00:01:55,797 --> 00:01:59,277
Click Open contact to check
his Do not disturb settings.

38
00:01:59,277 --> 00:02:03,317
Only switch it off if Mason has
actually agreed to hear from you.

39
00:02:03,317 --> 00:02:05,803
If he opted out, the workflow was right,

40
00:02:05,803 --> 00:02:09,345
and email or a phone call is
the better way to reach him.

41
00:02:10,195 --> 00:02:12,954
Now filter by status, and choose Failed.

42
00:02:12,954 --> 00:02:16,196
Ethan Walker's email
failed because it bounced.

43
00:02:16,196 --> 00:02:17,645
His mailbox was full.

44
00:02:17,645 --> 00:02:22,059
The fix here is outside the
workflow: confirm his email address,

45
00:02:22,059 --> 00:02:24,060
or reach him by text instead.

46
00:02:24,911 --> 00:02:29,015
Finally, a status that worries
people but shouldn't: Waiting.

47
00:02:29,015 --> 00:02:31,975
Olivia is simply paused
on the one-day wait.

48
00:02:31,975 --> 00:02:35,339
The details tell you exactly
when she'll continue.

49
00:02:35,339 --> 00:02:36,549
Nothing is broken.

50
00:02:36,549 --> 00:02:38,568
The workflow is doing its job.

51
00:02:39,417 --> 00:02:40,547
Here's a pro tip.

52
00:02:40,547 --> 00:02:42,274
Don't wait for complaints.

53
00:02:42,274 --> 00:02:47,590
Once a week, open your busiest workflows,
filter the logs by Skipped and Failed,

54
00:02:47,590 --> 00:02:49,051
and look for patterns.

55
00:02:49,051 --> 00:02:54,500
A wrong form, a bad number, or a missing
custom value is much easier to fix early.

56
00:02:55,368 --> 00:02:58,002
That's the end of the automation module.

57
00:02:58,002 --> 00:03:01,822
You can now build, test and
fix workflows with confidence.

58
00:03:01,822 --> 00:03:04,918
Next, in Module 10, we'll
explore AI in Kyntlo,

59
00:03:04,918 --> 00:03:09,660
from chatbots that answer your leads,
to AI steps inside your workflows.

60
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:10,582
See you there!
